  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Technology-Transfer Dossier",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Technology-Transfer Dossier\"**\n\nThe site is set as the front page of a patent document. A white sheet sits under an ink-blue bibliographic band; the sheet is divided by hairline rules into fields, and each field is numbered with a bracketed INID-style code in mono: (11) the name, (72) the researcher, (73) the companies as titulares, (57) the abstract, (74) the profiles. The codes are wayfinding, not a claim to patents. Below the fields, Fig. 1 is a line drawing of the 2005–2026 trajectory with numeral circles on leader lines that hand the reader into the period register, exactly as a patent figure's reference numerals lead into the description.\n\nThe density is that of a printed document: compact rows, tight ruled lists, a reading column that never exceeds about 62–80ch. Nothing floats or lifts. Hierarchy comes from type width and weight (condensed heavy Archivo for names and titles), from rule weight (2px ink rules open a sheet or a period; 1px rules divide fields; lighter 1px rules divide rows), and from the one reserved colour, the violet date-stamp, which marks only what is ongoing. The dark theme is a cyanotype: the same sheet printed in blue, not an inverted UI.\n\nThe world refuses the academic template of photo plus bio plus cards. The photo exists, but as an 88×110 greyscale plate inside field (72), framed by a 1px ink line like an inventor's mark.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Ink-blue band masthead carrying (19) institution and the PT/EN and theme controls.",
      "Bracketed mono field codes inline at the start of headings, never as separate eyebrows.",
      "Hairline-ruled fields and registers; no cards, no drop shadows.",
      "Condensed Archivo display, Source Serif reading text, JetBrains Mono for codes, refs, years and data.",
      "Violet stamp reserved for live / ongoing state.",
      "Line-drawn figures with numeral circles and leader lines into registers; partial data dashed and labelled."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Live Stamp Rule",
        "body": "Violet means \"ongoing\" and nothing else. It is never used for links, hover, emphasis, headings or decoration; if a thing is not currently running, it is not violet.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Band Rule",
        "body": "Ink blue as a filled surface appears only in the masthead band. Elsewhere blue is a line, a wash or a data tint.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Key Square Rule",
        "body": "Area colours are applied only as the 2px stroke of a hollow square marker (11–14px) next to the area's name; they never fill text, rows or backgrounds.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Inline Code Rule",
        "body": "A field code sits inside its heading, on the same baseline, before the heading text: `(73) Titulares — empresas co-fundadas`, `Fig. 1 Trajetória 2005–2026`. It is never a standalone line above a heading.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono Is Data Rule",
        "body": "JetBrains Mono is used only for codes, references, years, periods, counts and figure values. Prose, names and headings are never set in mono.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Condensed Name Rule",
        "body": "The narrow width axis (78–80%) is reserved for the display name/title and the bibliographic figures; everything else is set at normal width.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Printed Sheet Rule",
        "body": "Nothing lifts off the sheet. If something needs separation, give it a rule; if it needs emphasis, give it weight or the band; never a shadow or a card.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do number every top-level field with a bracketed mono code placed inline at the start of its heading.",
      "Do separate with rules: 2px ink to open a sheet or period, 1px field rule between fields, 1px row rule between rows.",
      "Do reserve the stamp violet for ongoing / live state only (stamp and ongoing ticks).",
      "Do set names and titles in condensed heavy Archivo, reading text in Source Serif 4, and codes, refs, years and data in JetBrains Mono.",
      "Do link a figure to its register with outlined numeral circles on leader lines, repeating the same numeral at the register entry.",
      "Do draw partial or incomplete data dashed and label it in words (\"parcial\" / \"partial\").",
      "Do give every interactive target at least 44px in its smallest dimension.",
      "Do redefine every colour token for the cyanotype theme rather than styling components per theme."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't place a field code or label as a standalone eyebrow line above a heading.",
      "Don't use cards, boxed panels or drop shadows; box-shadow is allowed only as a zero-blur hairline or flat highlight bleed.",
      "Don't use violet for links, hover, emphasis or decoration.",
      "Don't fill surfaces with ink blue outside the masthead band.",
      "Don't set prose, names or headings in mono.",
      "Don't fill text or rows with area colours; use them only as hollow-square key markers."
    ]
  }
}